# Project Conventions

## State Management: Riverpod (no StatefulWidget)

NEVER use `StatefulWidget`. Use `ConsumerWidget` / `ConsumerStatefulWidget` from `flutter_riverpod` and lift state into providers/notifiers.

```dart
// BAD
class Counter extends StatefulWidget { ... }
class _CounterState extends State<Counter> {
  int count = 0;
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text('$count');
}

// GOOD
final counterProvider = NotifierProvider<CounterNotifier, int>(CounterNotifier.new);

class CounterNotifier extends Notifier<int> {
  @override
  int build() => 0;
  void increment() => state++;
}

class Counter extends ConsumerWidget {
  const Counter({super.key});
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final count = ref.watch(counterProvider);
    return Text('$count');
  }
}
```

Prefer `Notifier` / `AsyncNotifier` over legacy `StateNotifier` / `ChangeNotifier`. Use `ref.watch` in `build`, `ref.read` for one-off actions.

## Navigation: GetX

Use `Get.to`, `Get.off`, `Get.offAll`, `Get.back`, named routes via `Get.toNamed`. Do NOT use `Navigator.push`/`MaterialPageRoute` directly.

```dart
// BAD
Navigator.of(context).push(MaterialPageRoute(builder: (_) => HomePage()));

// GOOD
Get.to(() => const HomePage());
Get.toNamed(Routes.home);
```

Define routes/pages in `lib/app/router/`. Keep `GetX` strictly for navigation/snackbars/dialogs — do NOT use `GetxController` or `Obx` for state (that belongs to Riverpod).

## Folder Structure

Place files according to this layout. Each feature follows clean-architecture layers (`data` / `domain` / `presentation`).

```
lib/
├── app/
│   ├── app.dart
│   ├── router/         # GetX routes, page bindings
│   ├── theme/
│   ├── config/
│   └── constants/
├── core/
│   ├── network/        # dio/http clients, interceptors
│   ├── storage/        # secure storage, prefs
│   ├── errors/         # Failure, Exception types
│   ├── services/
│   ├── utils/
│   ├── widgets/        # cross-feature shared widgets
│   └── extensions/
├── features/
│   └── <feature>/
│       ├── data/
│       │   ├── models/
│       │   ├── repositories/   # repo impls
│       │   └── datasources/    # remote/local
│       ├── domain/
│       │   ├── entities/
│       │   ├── repositories/   # abstract contracts
│       │   └── usecases/
│       ├── presentation/
│       │   ├── pages/
│       │   ├── widgets/
│       │   ├── controllers/    # Riverpod notifiers
│       │   └── state/          # state classes / providers
│       └── <feature>_di.dart   # provider wiring
├── shared/
│   ├── widgets/
│   ├── models/
│   ├── enums/
│   └── helpers/
├── main.dart
└── bootstrap.dart
```

Rules:
- `domain` must not import from `data` or `presentation`.
- `presentation` depends on `domain` (not `data` directly).
- Cross-feature reusable code goes in `core/` or `shared/`, never in another feature.
- Riverpod providers for a feature live in `presentation/state/` and are wired in `<feature>_di.dart`.
